<rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom" xmlns:media="http://search.yahoo.com/mrss/" xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/"><channel><language>en</language><title>News from Europe - Latest world headlines and daily news - France 24</title><description>FRANCE 24 explores events across Europe, including in the 27 member states of the European Union and the United Kingdom. Follow our on-the-ground reports, interviews and analyses of the events affecting social and political life on the Continent and Europe’s role in the world.</description><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/</link><lastBuildDate>Fri, 16 Oct 2026 13:13:34 GMT</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/rss" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><category>Talking Europe</category><title>'America, with this president, is not our ally. Trump is a liar': French MEP Bernard Guetta</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/talking-europe/20261016-america-with-this-president-is-not-our-ally-trump-is-a-liar-french-mep-bernard-guetta</link><description>
Our guest is veteran French journalist and commentator Bernard Guetta, who is a Member of the European Parliament for the centrist Renew group. He tells the programme that Donald Trump is "a liar, because he tried to tell the American people that Zelensky and the Ukrainian resistance were responsible for the price of diesel. This is a pure lie. He (Trump) is responsible because he started the war with Iran." Guetta goes on to say that "without American intelligence sharing, Ukraine is weaker and weaker. That's terrible, to see the president of the United States giving a hand to Putin against Ukraine."
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/54ceab9e-c8a4-11f1-b31f-6313a763b466/w:1024/p:16x9/ENTK-TALKING-EU1-GUETTA-261017-2027-Ep-7-transfer.png"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/54ceab9e-c8a4-11f1-b31f-6313a763b466/w:1024/p:16x9/ENTK-TALKING-EU1-GUETTA-261017-2027-Ep-7-transfer.png" type="image/png" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">15b7bc28-c653-11f1-8f3d-97eea9bcf669</guid><pubDate>Fri, 16 Oct 2026 12:55:38 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Armen GEORGIAN</dc:creator></item><item><category>Talking Europe</category><title>EU and Canada seek closer ties: Will Canada become the EU's first associate member?</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/talking-europe/20261016-eu-and-canada-seek-closer-ties-will-canada-become-the-eu-s-first-associate-member</link><description>
As the international context becomes more challenging for the European Union, the bloc is looking to boost its ties with like-minded allies. Canada is part of that architecture that the EU says it wants to build. The big news of EU Commission President Ursula von der Leyen's State of the Union speech in September was that Canada could become an associate member – an arrangement that does not exist for the EU's partners at the moment.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/0ee425ac-c893-11f1-84f5-2d1c143cdef3/w:1024/p:16x9/261014-FR24-Talking-EU-1-div.png"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/0ee425ac-c893-11f1-84f5-2d1c143cdef3/w:1024/p:16x9/261014-FR24-Talking-EU-1-div.png" type="image/png" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">8de8b97c-c653-11f1-9540-3fc578080398</guid><pubDate>Fri, 16 Oct 2026 12:04:22 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Armen GEORGIAN</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>UK bookstores scramble as Sally Rooney's novels pulled over Palestine Action support</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261016-uk-bookstores-scramble-as-sally-rooney-novels-pulled-over-palestine-action-support</link><description>
Critically acclaimed Irish novelist Sally Rooney's announcement that her books could no longer be sold in the UK due to her support for proscribed group Palestine Action has left British booksellers rushing to stock up on her works before distributors run out. The British government's ban on the group, which practiced non-violent direct action and sabotage against UK military assets believed to be working with the Israeli government, makes support for Palestine Action punishable by up to 14 years in prison.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/0420bd06-c924-11f1-923c-4dd8ac2cf3bf/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-14T151142Z-1755491356-RC233OAKW8RS-RTRMADP-3-BRITAIN-SALLY-ROONEY.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/0420bd06-c924-11f1-923c-4dd8ac2cf3bf/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-14T151142Z-1755491356-RC233OAKW8RS-RTRMADP-3-BRITAIN-SALLY-ROONEY.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">206a3ea2-c923-11f1-809f-7bc78db3cd1e</guid><pubDate>Fri, 16 Oct 2026 06:15:10 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/0420bd06-c924-11f1-923c-4dd8ac2cf3bf/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-14T151142Z-1755491356-RC233OAKW8RS-RTRMADP-3-BRITAIN-SALLY-ROONEY.jpg">© Henry Nicholls, Reuters</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>Live: Ukraine is ‘dependent’ on Starlink for intercepting Russian drones, Zelensky says</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261016-live-trump-calls-renewed-ukraine-attacks-on-russian-oil-refineries-a-disgrace</link><description>
Ukraine depends on US satellite intelligence service Starlink to intercept jet-powered Russian drones, Ukrainian President Volodymyr Zelensky said at an EU leaders summit in Brussels Friday. Kyiv was angered this week by disruptions to the critical satellite system hampering its military's ability to counter intense Russian bombardment ahead of the winter months. Follow our liveblog for the latest developments.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/8c48c988-c958-11f1-b364-6313a763b466/w:1024/p:16x9/000-D3GY8GV.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/8c48c988-c958-11f1-b364-6313a763b466/w:1024/p:16x9/000-D3GY8GV.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">ec95e172-c903-11f1-b093-3b96d215f849</guid><pubDate>Fri, 16 Oct 2026 01:50:10 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/8c48c988-c958-11f1-b364-6313a763b466/w:1024/p:16x9/000-D3GY8GV.jpg">© Nicolas Tucat, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>Minibus crashes into train at French Channel Tunnel entrance, injuring 19</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261016-19-injured-as-minibus-crashes-into-train-at-channel-tunnel-entrance</link><description>
Nineteen people were injured Thursday when a minibus carrying truck drivers crashed into a vehicle shuttle train at the French entrance to the Channel Tunnel near Calais, forcing a 90-minute suspension of shuttle services. Two people were hospitalised with serious but non-life-threatening injuries, French authorities said.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/6a8daece-71cc-11f0-9526-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/000-397M8WK.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/6a8daece-71cc-11f0-9526-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/000-397M8WK.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">f99b5af8-c8fb-11f1-b305-c7c144120c8c</guid><pubDate>Fri, 16 Oct 2026 00:53:16 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/6a8daece-71cc-11f0-9526-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/000-397M8WK.jpg">© Sameer Al-Doumy, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>France and Germany agree to ease EU car emissions rules in new deal</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261015-france-and-germany-agree-to-ease-eu-car-emissions-rules-in-new-deal</link><description>
Paris and Berlin on Friday confirmed their deal aimed at protecting Europe's struggling automotive sector, having reached agreements on the flashpoint issues of EU car emissions and "made in Europe" components. A draft deal reviewed Thursday showed the two countries backing looser EU emissions rules for carmakers.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/af286218-c8e7-11f1-8247-2d1c143cdef3/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26270718148994.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/af286218-c8e7-11f1-8247-2d1c143cdef3/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26270718148994.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">fd324f7c-c8f2-11f1-a500-2b19cb1aea8f</guid><pubDate>Thu, 15 Oct 2026 23:48:57 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/af286218-c8e7-11f1-8247-2d1c143cdef3/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26270718148994.jpg">© Michael Sohn, AP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>Zelensky rallies European allies as US support for Ukraine wanes</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261015-zelensky-rallies-european-allies-as-us-support-for-ukraine-wanes</link><description>
Ukrainian President Volodymyr Zelensky sought European backing Thursday after vowing to resume strikes on Russian oil refineries despite US President Donald Trump’s demands to stop. Tensions between Kyiv and Washington have escalated in recent days over sanctions, energy infrastructure attacks and restrictions on satellite communications.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/28bbd5dc-c8d5-11f1-aec7-2d1c143cdef3/w:1024/p:16x9/80c62e6fc13f8d6a5641fe9e16da5b4e0ca12147.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/28bbd5dc-c8d5-11f1-aec7-2d1c143cdef3/w:1024/p:16x9/80c62e6fc13f8d6a5641fe9e16da5b4e0ca12147.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">fd8e39fa-c8ec-11f1-a26b-7beb10019f07</guid><pubDate>Thu, 15 Oct 2026 23:06:00 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/28bbd5dc-c8d5-11f1-aec7-2d1c143cdef3/w:1024/p:16x9/80c62e6fc13f8d6a5641fe9e16da5b4e0ca12147.jpg">© AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>A propos</category><title>Sally Rooney's books cannot be sold in UK amid Palestine Action ban, publisher says</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/a-propos/20261015-sally-rooney-books-cannot-be-sold-in-uk-amid-palestine-action-ban-publisher</link><description>
Irish author Sally Rooney can no longer sell her books in the UK because of her support for the activist group Palestine Action, her publisher Faber said on Wednesday. Rooney has previously expressed her support for the group, which was banned as a "terrorist" organisation by the UK government in July 2025. It is not banned in Ireland, where Rooney lives. FRANCE 24's Sharon Gaffney speaks with Alan Greene, Professor of Constitutional Law and Human Rights at the Birmingham Law School.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/5b769a14-c940-11f1-8e34-2d1c143cdef3/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-c3daade0.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/5b769a14-c940-11f1-8e34-2d1c143cdef3/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-c3daade0.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">82159a16-c8dd-11f1-aa7d-07fd22e88b92</guid><pubDate>Thu, 15 Oct 2026 21:15:11 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Sharon GAFFNEY</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>'It is clear that sooner or later we will have European casualties', Romanian MEP</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/it-is-clear-that-sooner-or-later-we-will-have-european-casualties-romanian-mep</link><description>
Rescuers searched on Thursday for seven missing sailors after drones struck two chemical tankers near Romania's Black Sea coast, setting them ablaze and raising fresh security concerns along a vital shipping route used by Ukraine. Speaking with FRANCE 24's Europe editor Armen Georgian, Nicolae Stefanuta, Romanian MEP and Co-Chair of the Group of the Greens, says that the Danube delta region is facing a more intense threat from Russia than Baltic States and that "it is clear that sooner or later we will have European casualties".
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/bc7eaac2-c8d2-11f1-b063-638c1c1f5fd6/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261015-211432-211932-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/bc7eaac2-c8d2-11f1-b063-638c1c1f5fd6/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261015-211432-211932-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">c1b2e1d4-c8d2-11f1-925f-cb689c3210d5</guid><pubDate>Thu, 15 Oct 2026 20:03:10 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Donald Trump 'openly financing Russia's war with Ukraine', Nobel peace laureate says</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/donald-trump-openly-financing-russia-s-war-with-ukraine-nobel-peace-laureate-says</link><description>
Speaking with FRANCE 24's Mark Owen, Nobel Peace laureate Oleksandra Matviichuk, Director of the Centre for Civil Liberties, says that with the diesel-supply deal with Moscow Donald Trump "is openly financing this war, by lifting sanctions is providing Russia with opportunities to earn more money" adding that "extra money will be converted in rockets and drones and additional deaths among the civilian population".
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/6dc8c71c-c8cf-11f1-b194-4dd8ac2cf3bf/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261015-210633-211324-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/6dc8c71c-c8cf-11f1-b194-4dd8ac2cf3bf/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261015-210633-211324-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">72e458d8-c8cf-11f1-b211-61fe1cac82d8</guid><pubDate>Thu, 15 Oct 2026 19:48:10 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Seven missing off Romania after latest Black Sea drone attacks</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/seven-missing-off-romania-after-latest-black-sea-drone-attacks</link><description>
Romania reported seven people missing on Thursday after two drone attacks on ships in the Black Sea, where several vessels have been hit recently in suspected fallout from the Ukraine war. The attacks are the latest in a series off the coast of Romania and neighbouring Bulgaria in recent weeks. FRANCE 24's Eliza Herbert reports.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/8d4a8504-c8c9-11f1-bf1b-4dd8ac2cf3bf/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261015-203417-203608-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/8d4a8504-c8c9-11f1-bf1b-4dd8ac2cf3bf/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261015-203417-203608-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">96ab9714-c8c9-11f1-8c3c-27acdd5cac97</guid><pubDate>Thu, 15 Oct 2026 19:04:12 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Albania's leader defies calls to resign as student protesters rampage in capital</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/albania-s-leader-defies-calls-to-resign-as-student-protesters-rampage-in-capital</link><description>
​Albanian Prime Minister Edi Rama on Thursday rejected calls to resign as thousands of student-led protesters smashed windows and fought running battles with riot police firing water cannon and tear gas in the capital. The demonstrators accuse officials of corruption and neglecting education and say they are angry about the sale of parts of Albania's southern coastline to a luxury resort development backed ​by US President ‌Donald Trump's son-in-law Jared Kushner. FRANCE 24's Emerald Maxwell reports
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/281c8484-c8c9-11f1-8ffe-d1d2c32ebb87/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261015-200906-201102-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/281c8484-c8c9-11f1-8ffe-d1d2c32ebb87/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261015-200906-201102-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">38d566e2-c8c9-11f1-b983-7f8e2f52719a</guid><pubDate>Thu, 15 Oct 2026 19:02:14 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>The Debate</category><title>Will Trump really pull the plug? Starlink restored but Ukraine's fate still uncertain</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-debate/20261015-will-trump-really-pull-the-plug-starlink-restored-but-ukraine-s-fate-still-uncertain</link><description>
Can a flick of a switch really be enough for Donald Trump and Elon Musk to end Ukraine's hopes of holding out against Russia? With Kyiv already reeling from daily strikes by Russia's new motor-powered drones, the US decision to slow SpaceX's Starlink service was felt immediately on Wednesday, when air raid warnings failed.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/0be3d78c-c8c3-11f1-936e-d1d2c32ebb87/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-15T074057Z-616239413-RC233OAF2BZE-RTRMADP-3-UKRAINE-CRISIS-DONETSK-REGION.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/0be3d78c-c8c3-11f1-936e-d1d2c32ebb87/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-15T074057Z-616239413-RC233OAF2BZE-RTRMADP-3-UKRAINE-CRISIS-DONETSK-REGION.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">b90d2078-c8c1-11f1-b4e2-b7b3e4e3c9a4</guid><pubDate>Thu, 15 Oct 2026 18:38:17 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>François PICARD</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>Why have US-Ukraine relations soured ahead of the midterms?</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261015-why-have-us-ukraine-relations-soured-ahead-of-the-midterms</link><description>
Ukraine's President Volodymyr Zelensky said he felt “betrayed” on Wednesday after access was seemingly restricted to US intelligence and Space X satellite services, raising new questions about US commitment to Ukraine. With Trump under pressure over rising fuel prices, is the White House hoping criticism of Kyiv can help shift the blame? 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b15f302e-c8ac-11f1-a90d-4dd8ac2cf3bf/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26281714511676.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b15f302e-c8ac-11f1-a90d-4dd8ac2cf3bf/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26281714511676.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">d58215b2-c8ab-11f1-95cb-9d4b1f97111e</guid><pubDate>Thu, 15 Oct 2026 17:54:08 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b15f302e-c8ac-11f1-a90d-4dd8ac2cf3bf/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26281714511676.jpg">© Julia Demaree Nikhinson, AP</source><dc:creator>Joanna YORK</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>'We're done': Ukraine resumes strikes on Russian oil refineries as 'only leverage' for peace talks</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261015-we-re-done-ukraine-resumes-strikes-on-russian-oil-refineries-as-only-leverage-for-peace-talks-1</link><description>
Delano D'Souza is pleased to welcome Peter Zalmayev, Founder and Director of the Eurasia Democracy Initiative, LIVE from Kyiv. As Zelensky declares Ukraine "done" with Trump's self-declared energy ceasefire and resumes strikes on Russian oil refineries, Zalmayev warns: "When you talk about the energy ceasefire, it presupposes two to be able to tango and to dance this dance." He challenges the legitimacy of Trump's unilateral announcement, made without agreement between Moscow and Kyiv, as Russia continues attacking Ukraine's energy infrastructure. Yet he cautions that Zelensky may need tactical restraint to preserve vital US support. Zalmayev also examines Western sanctions, frozen Russian assets, and Washington's pursuit of economic normalization with Moscow without meaningful Russian concessions.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/58af4524-c8af-11f1-8d33-6313a763b466/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261015-130211-131029-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/58af4524-c8af-11f1-8d33-6313a763b466/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261015-130211-131029-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">a36ed962-c8af-11f1-bc01-231790081c82</guid><pubDate>Thu, 15 Oct 2026 16:14:25 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>NATO to address drone attacks in the Black Sea after seven missing off Romania</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261015-seven-missing-off-romania-after-latest-black-sea-drone-attacks</link><description>
NATO will put drone strikes in the Black Sea on its agenda at a meeting next week, officials said Thursday, following two new attacks and the disappearance of seven people. Incidents involving civilian vessels in the Black Sea have been on the rise off the coasts of Bulgaria and Romania in a suspected spillover from Russia’s war in Ukraine.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/e42d5b20-c8a7-11f1-a87e-d1d2c32ebb87/w:1024/p:16x9/9e825dda6ecaf41ed8fa636033ec60663423d630.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/e42d5b20-c8a7-11f1-a87e-d1d2c32ebb87/w:1024/p:16x9/9e825dda6ecaf41ed8fa636033ec60663423d630.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">45d51de6-c89d-11f1-9236-07b36ca1617f</guid><pubDate>Thu, 15 Oct 2026 13:35:22 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/e42d5b20-c8a7-11f1-a87e-d1d2c32ebb87/w:1024/p:16x9/9e825dda6ecaf41ed8fa636033ec60663423d630.jpg">© Handout from Ministry of Interior Bulgaria via AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>Student protests spread in Albania as demonstrators call for PM resignation</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261015-student-protests-escalate-in-albania-as-demonstrators-call-for-pm-resignation</link><description>
Clashes broke out between demonstrators and police for the third consecutive day on Thursday in Albania, with Prime Minister Edi Rama condemning the “chaos” that caused damage to government buildings. Thousands of protesters are calling for Rama's resignation and better studying conditions for Albanian students.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c62f1866-c893-11f1-bbdd-2d1c143cdef3/w:1024/p:16x9/c5d39ddd12d0832bc704ebd4b58a7ca0b7ebbee6.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c62f1866-c893-11f1-bbdd-2d1c143cdef3/w:1024/p:16x9/c5d39ddd12d0832bc704ebd4b58a7ca0b7ebbee6.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">c70462d2-c893-11f1-9ecb-4d9714b03f50</guid><pubDate>Thu, 15 Oct 2026 12:27:24 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c62f1866-c893-11f1-bbdd-2d1c143cdef3/w:1024/p:16x9/c5d39ddd12d0832bc704ebd4b58a7ca0b7ebbee6.jpg">© Adnan Beci, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>Russia detains independent outlet Novaya Gazeta editor Sergei Sokolov</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261015-russia-detains-novaya-gazeta-editor-in-chief-sergei-sokolov-after-home-search</link><description>
Sergei Sokolov, the editor-in-chief of Russia's independent newspaper Novaya Gazeta, was detained and taken for questioning on Thursday after authorities searched his home, the newspaper said.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/cd8c2f0c-c88b-11f1-8592-2d1c143cdef3/w:1024/p:16x9/000-D3D79KE.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/cd8c2f0c-c88b-11f1-8592-2d1c143cdef3/w:1024/p:16x9/000-D3D79KE.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">f0ab8140-c88b-11f1-9849-0fbb85ce41e0</guid><pubDate>Thu, 15 Oct 2026 11:39:31 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/cd8c2f0c-c88b-11f1-8592-2d1c143cdef3/w:1024/p:16x9/000-D3D79KE.jpg">© Igor Ivanko, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Press Review</category><title>'American abandonment' threatens Ukraine's civilians in war against Russia</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/press-review/20261015-american-abandonment-threatens-ukraine-s-civilians-in-war-against-russia</link><description>
PRESS REVIEW – Thursday, October 15: First, reported Starlink disruptions in Ukraine make the European front pages. Next, US papers go into more detail about the situation. Also, an unusual alliance forms in Germany between far-right and far-left parties. Meanwhile, the winners of the Wildlife Photographer of the Year awards have been announced. Finally, Finland flaunts its smelly islands.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/1ee85026-c885-11f1-9705-2d1c143cdef3/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-5116b1de.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/1ee85026-c885-11f1-9705-2d1c143cdef3/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-5116b1de.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">804e3c42-c865-11f1-bc3e-3114adfafbf4</guid><pubDate>Thu, 15 Oct 2026 11:09:09 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Emily BOYLE</dc:creator></item><item><category>Focus</category><title>War in Ukraine: Kyiv residents decry shortage of bomb shelters</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/focus/20261015-war-in-ukraine-kyiv-residents-decry-shortage-of-bomb-shelters</link><description>
Kyiv's mayor, Vitaly Klitschko, has advised those residents who can "temporarily relocate" for the winter to do so. That advice has been met with derision at best from many residents, who say his administration is responsible for failing to better prepare the Ukrainian capital for Russian attacks. In particular, they complain of a severe shortage of adequate bomb shelters.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/8ff98ea6-c876-11f1-99ac-6313a763b466/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-5eb8f3a5.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/8ff98ea6-c876-11f1-99ac-6313a763b466/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-5eb8f3a5.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">911c1920-c7cc-11f1-8e80-b783564a2256</guid><pubDate>Thu, 15 Oct 2026 09:50:30 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Gulliver CRAGG</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>EU leaders head into high-stakes budget battle as elections loom</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/eu-leaders-head-into-high-stakes-budget-battle-as-elections-loom</link><description>
EU leaders head to a summit on Thursday seeking a deal on the bloc’s nearly €2 trillion budget for 2028-2034 by Christmas amid deep divisions over spending and fears that upcoming elections, particularly in France, could strengthen eurosceptic forces.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/0aa7737e-c83c-11f1-af7d-638c1c1f5fd6/w:1024/p:16x9/90bd5f4c90f09eb957948de43a7ce1797745125f.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/0aa7737e-c83c-11f1-af7d-638c1c1f5fd6/w:1024/p:16x9/90bd5f4c90f09eb957948de43a7ce1797745125f.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">cdfb3e8e-c85d-11f1-8339-0d5a9df05665</guid><pubDate>Thu, 15 Oct 2026 06:03:27 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>France 'can no longer finance' Ukraine, far-right presidential frontrunner Le Pen says</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261015-france-can-no-longer-finance-ukraine-far-right-candidate-marine-le-pen-says</link><description>
Far-right leader and presidential candidate Marine Le Pen said on Wednesday that France could no longer afford to fund Ukraine, citing the country's high deficit and weak economic growth.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/212d5b6c-c85b-11f1-910c-d1d2c32ebb87/w:1024/p:16x9/000-D3B329N.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/212d5b6c-c85b-11f1-910c-d1d2c32ebb87/w:1024/p:16x9/000-D3B329N.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">8c9d7838-c85a-11f1-8246-25553aadac69</guid><pubDate>Thu, 15 Oct 2026 05:49:13 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/212d5b6c-c85b-11f1-910c-d1d2c32ebb87/w:1024/p:16x9/000-D3B329N.jpg">© Nicolas Tucas, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>Zelensky meets NATO chief and EU leaders in push to apply 'real pressure' on Russia</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261015-ukraine-live-romania-probes-possible-drone-attack-on-tanker</link><description>
Ukrainian President Volodymyr Zelensky arrived in Brussels Thursday to rally support at a meeting with NATO chief Mark Rutte the same day, and a summit with EU leaders to follow Friday. Earlier, Zelensky asked the United States not to stand with Moscow and called for "honesty" after Kyiv said it had been betrayed by Washington's intelligence-sharing gaps. Follow our liveblog to see how the day's events unfolded.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/2ea45b56-c7f7-11f1-a634-d1d2c32ebb87/w:1024/p:16x9/000-D3AQ7YY.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/2ea45b56-c7f7-11f1-a634-d1d2c32ebb87/w:1024/p:16x9/000-D3AQ7YY.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">2419a9ac-c81a-11f1-9243-6b277543ded8</guid><pubDate>Thu, 15 Oct 2026 03:52:46 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/2ea45b56-c7f7-11f1-a634-d1d2c32ebb87/w:1024/p:16x9/000-D3AQ7YY.jpg">© Henry Nicholls, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>Macron urges EU to agree to long-term budget by Christmas and ahead of elections</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261015-eu-leaders-head-for-showdown-over-bloc-budget</link><description>
French President Emmanuel Macron urged EU leaders on Thursday to reach a deal on the bloc’s nearly €2 trillion budget by Christmas, warning that elections in France and other European countries in 2027 could leave little room for compromise as divisions deepen over spending priorities and funding.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/0aa7737e-c83c-11f1-af7d-638c1c1f5fd6/w:1024/p:16x9/90bd5f4c90f09eb957948de43a7ce1797745125f.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/0aa7737e-c83c-11f1-af7d-638c1c1f5fd6/w:1024/p:16x9/90bd5f4c90f09eb957948de43a7ce1797745125f.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">0b9d276a-c83c-11f1-9b34-91703ebeeb06</guid><pubDate>Thu, 15 Oct 2026 01:59:23 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/0aa7737e-c83c-11f1-af7d-638c1c1f5fd6/w:1024/p:16x9/90bd5f4c90f09eb957948de43a7ce1797745125f.jpg">© John Thys, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>Albania protests turn violent as protestors demand PM Rama's resignation</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261014-albania-protests-protestors-demand-pm-rama-resignation</link><description>
Anti-government protests in Albania’s capital Tirana turned violent for a second consecutive night on Wednesday, leaving several government buildings damaged and at least one ablaze. As thousands demanded improved university conditions and the government's resignation, Albanian Prime Minister Edi Rama said he would not step down.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/fbf524c2-c820-11f1-9100-2d1c143cdef3/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-14T222222Z-1949817444-RC233OAJSBMG-RTRMADP-3-ALBANIA-PROTESTS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/fbf524c2-c820-11f1-9100-2d1c143cdef3/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-14T222222Z-1949817444-RC233OAJSBMG-RTRMADP-3-ALBANIA-PROTESTS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">b967b1f4-c81d-11f1-a7c2-d51d50e7e553</guid><pubDate>Wed, 14 Oct 2026 22:35:08 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/fbf524c2-c820-11f1-9100-2d1c143cdef3/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-14T222222Z-1949817444-RC233OAJSBMG-RTRMADP-3-ALBANIA-PROTESTS.jpg">© Florion Goga, Reuters</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>French anti-terror investigators probe True Crime Community link to school shooting</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/french-anti-terror-investigators-probe-true-crime-community-link-to-school-shooting</link><description>
The French anti-terrorism prosecutor has taken ​over the investigation into a school shooting near Marseille, after an initial probe found the 14-year-old suspect appeared to belong to ​a ‌group called the True Crime ⁠Community. Two teachers were shot and wounded, after a student opened fire with ⁠a hunting rifle that had been hidden inside a guitar case. FRANCE 24's Sharon Gaffney speaks with Alexandre Rodde, security consultant, researcher and author of the report "Understanding nihilistic violent extremism and the True Crime Community in France".
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/295d0fd0-c88d-11f1-b1b5-d1d2c32ebb87/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-af39ad88.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/295d0fd0-c88d-11f1-b1b5-d1d2c32ebb87/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-af39ad88.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">01338ce0-c811-11f1-bf27-b3491a10e8e5</guid><pubDate>Wed, 14 Oct 2026 20:58:31 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>What is Starshield, SpaceX's military version of Starlink?</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261014-what-is-starshield-spacex-s-military-version-of-starlink</link><description>
Elon Musk’s ⁠SpaceX restricted “military-grade” ​Starlink services overnight into Wednesday, hampering Ukrainian drone strike missions and air defences, Ukraine reported. In response, Musk said that the US government was behind any slowdown in Ukraine's Starshield system. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/d6d59c4e-c807-11f1-a293-4dd8ac2cf3bf/w:1024/p:16x9/Starshield.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/d6d59c4e-c807-11f1-a293-4dd8ac2cf3bf/w:1024/p:16x9/Starshield.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">9675ed00-c809-11f1-8cec-2b55fa072aed</guid><pubDate>Wed, 14 Oct 2026 20:15:58 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/d6d59c4e-c807-11f1-a293-4dd8ac2cf3bf/w:1024/p:16x9/Starshield.jpg">© ZUMA Press Wire via Reuters Connect, Gene Blevins</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Nord Stream may have been lawful target, argue lawyers for Ukrainian accused of bombing</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/nord-stream-may-have-been-lawful-target-argue-lawyers-for-ukrainian-accused-of-bombing</link><description>
Lawyers for a Ukrainian ex-military officer accused of leading the bombing of Russia's Nord Stream ​pipeline in September 2022 argued at the start of his trial in Germany on Wednesday that "an aggressor's infrastructure" may have been a lawful target. FRANCE 24's Juliette Brown reports.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/9680d490-c804-11f1-9a9a-4dd8ac2cf3bf/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261014-211506-211649-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/9680d490-c804-11f1-9a9a-4dd8ac2cf3bf/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261014-211506-211649-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">9b9d2a14-c804-11f1-9cd4-bd6088dee01f</guid><pubDate>Wed, 14 Oct 2026 19:56:42 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Starlink restriction 'no surprise' after Musk condemned Ukraine strikes on Russian data centres</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/starlink-restriction-no-surprise-after-musk-condemned-ukraine-strikes-on-russian-data-centres</link><description>
Restrictions reported by Ukraine on its use of the US satellite internet system Starlink have exposed Kyiv's reliance on the technology for both offensive and defensive operations in its fight against Russia'a invasion, analysts and observers say. Speaking with FRANCE 24's Mark Owen, David Galbreath Professor of War and Technology at the University of Bath, says that "we always knew that allowing a private organisation like Starlink to have such a big impact on the combat operations in Ukraine was going to be challenging", explaining that "it is no surprise" that Starlink services had been throttled after SpaceX boss Elon Musk called the targeting by Ukrainian drones of data services in Russia "a step too far". 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/7652471c-c804-11f1-ac63-6313a763b466/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261014-210507-211251-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/7652471c-c804-11f1-ac63-6313a763b466/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261014-210507-211251-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">7b7c5e62-c804-11f1-98f3-2dea6aa53833</guid><pubDate>Wed, 14 Oct 2026 19:49:17 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>Ukraine says Starlink restricted operations overnight, disrupting military missions</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261014-ukraine-says-starlink-restricted-operations-overnight-disrupting-military-missions</link><description>
Elon Musk's Starlink imposed restrictions on the operation of internet terminals in Ukraine overnight, disrupting military missions, an adviser to the Ukrainian president said on Wednesday. The official said Ukraine was given no prior warning about the restrictions to the satellite system it relies on for battlefield operations.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/9dc465e0-c7ab-11f1-8b0a-29a2e29ae696/w:1024/p:16x9/000-D38A7G3.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/9dc465e0-c7ab-11f1-8b0a-29a2e29ae696/w:1024/p:16x9/000-D38A7G3.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">9b26d3c6-c7ac-11f1-967a-c1ef70811b87</guid><pubDate>Wed, 14 Oct 2026 09:14:29 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/9dc465e0-c7ab-11f1-8b0a-29a2e29ae696/w:1024/p:16x9/000-D38A7G3.jpg">© Yasuyoshi Chiba, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item></channel></rss>
